From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:47:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Build render units on demand with a
 lazy PB heap

Every VM that renders even once builds all its render units at its
first render, as pinned kernel memory: two full units of 312.7 MiB,
each with a 256 MiB PB heap, and six compact units of 50.7 MiB. That
is 929.9 MiB for every GL or Vulkan client, the compositor and the
shell included, and a closed client's units stay until other clients'
renders take over every unit it last used.

Make g16_resident_lazy default to 2 and g16_pb_lazy default to 1. A
VM's first render then builds only its two full units, the others are
built by a worker when it has more render commands outstanding than
units, and the full units back 32 MiB of their PB heap window, growing
in SUBMIT to three times the blocks their renders were seen holding, or
to the whole window once a render held three quarters of its manager.

RESULT: on a J604 with 1.1072 booted with these two values on its
command line, the idle desktop held 715.0 MiB of pinned GPU memory
against 1864.7 MiB at the old defaults, and a render.light client at
depth 64 added 487.1 MiB while open against 935.2 MiB. In two blocks on
that boot render.light at depth 1 took 187.15 us against 189.6 us, and
render.light at depths 8 and 64, a 1080p fill, 1440p geometry and
render.heavy each stayed within 0.5 % of the old defaults. The boot
reached a working desktop with no fault line.

aurora.g16_resident_lazy=0 aurora.g16_pb_lazy=0 on the command line
return to every unit and the whole heap at the first render.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index 4669e904d6..2fda47d1f5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -1606,8 +1606,8 @@ pub(crate) fn pb_heap16() -> bool {
     "G16: back the PB heap of the full render units 0 and 1 with 16 MiB (128 blocks) as the compact units, instead of 256 MiB each (default 0; latched at the first render unit built, set it as a module option)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_pb_lazy` (0644, default 0; latched at its first read).
-static PB_LAZY: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_pb_lazy` (0644, default 1; latched at its first read).
+static PB_LAZY: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(1);
 /// 0 until latched, then the latched value plus one.
 static PB_LAZY_LATCH: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
 
@@ -1650,7 +1650,7 @@ pub(crate) fn pb_lazy() -> Option<u32> {
     PB_LAZY_PARM,
     PB_LAZY,
     "g16_pb_lazy",
-    "G16: back the full render units' PB heap lazily from a floor of N blocks (128 KiB each; 1 = 256 = 32 MiB) and grow it in SUBMIT to three times the blocks in use, or to the whole window once a render held 3/4 of its manager (default 0: whole heap at build; latched at the first read, set it as a module option)"
+    "G16: back the full render units' PB heap lazily from a floor of N blocks (128 KiB each; 1 = 256 = 32 MiB) and grow it in SUBMIT to three times the blocks in use, or to the whole window once a render held 3/4 of its manager (default 1; 0: whole heap at build; latched at the first read, set it as a module option)"
 );
 
 /// Storage of `g16_cwork_pack` (0644, default 0; latched at its first read).
@@ -2792,8 +2792,8 @@ pub(crate) fn bridge() -> u32 {
     "G16: enable the GPU-to-fabric bridge before the firmware runs, at start and at every wake, as macOS does (default 1; 0 leaves iBoot's values: the GFX domain then never powers off at idle)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_resident_lazy` (0644, default 0; read when a VM builds its render units).
-static RESIDENT_LAZY: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_resident_lazy` (0644, default 2; read when a VM builds its render units).
+static RESIDENT_LAZY: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(2);
 
 /// A VM's first render builds only the two full render units; the compact ones are built in
 /// SUBMIT, one at a time, when the VM has more render commands outstanding than units.
@@ -2813,7 +2813,7 @@ pub(crate) fn resident_lazy_async() -> bool {
     RESIDENT_LAZY_PARM,
     RESIDENT_LAZY,
     "g16_resident_lazy",
-    "G16: a VM's first render builds only its two full render units; the others are built when it queues deeper: 1 in SUBMIT, 2 by a worker (default 0: all at the first render; read when a VM builds units)"
+    "G16: a VM's first render builds only its two full render units; the others are built when it queues deeper: 1 in SUBMIT, 2 by a worker (default 2; 0: all at the first render; read when a VM builds units)"
 );
 
 /// Storage of `g16_loader_macos` (0644, default 7; read once, when initdata is built).
